Relevant columns and their potential usage for answering the business question  
• countries.country_name: country filter (‘France’).  
• countries.country_id: joins to customers.  
• customers.cust_id: joins to sales.  
• customers.country_id: connects each customer to a country.  
• sales.amount_sold: the actual sales value to aggregate.  
• sales.time_id: joins to times to know year / month.  
• sales.cust_id: joins to customers so we can restrict to French customers.  
• promotions.promo_id / promotions.promo_total_id: let us keep only rows where promo_total_id = 1.  
• channels.channel_id / channels.channel_total_id: let us keep only rows where channel_total_id = 1.  
• times.calendar_year, times.calendar_month_number: identify 2019, 2020, 2021 and the month.  
• currency.country, currency.year, currency.month, currency.to_us: turn local‐currency sales into USD (multiply amount_sold by to_us).  

Typical conditions that will be needed  
1. countries.country_name = 'France'  
2. promotions.promo_total_id = 1  
3. channels.channel_total_id = 1  
4. times.calendar_year IN (2019, 2020)  ––– for the historical data  
5. times.calendar_year = 2021           ––– for the projected data  

Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (from very simple to progressively richer joins) to inspect the values you will need.  All use SELECT … DISTINCT … LIMIT 20 with short result sets for safety.

```sql
-- 1. What is the country_id for France?
SELECT DISTINCT country_id
FROM countries
WHERE country_name = 'France'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show a handful of French customers (cust_id and names).
SELECT DISTINCT c.cust_id,
       c.cust_first_name || ' ' || c.cust_last_name AS full_name
FROM customers AS c
JOIN countries  AS co ON c.country_id = co.country_id
WHERE co.country_name = 'France'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Distinct promotion IDs whose promo_total_id = 1
SELECT DISTINCT promo_id
FROM promotions
WHERE promo_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Distinct channel IDs whose channel_total_id = 1
SELECT DISTINCT channel_id
FROM channels
WHERE channel_total_id = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Check French sales rows in 2019–2020 (raw amounts before currency conversion).
SELECT DISTINCT s.cust_id,
       s.time_id,
       s.amount_sold
FROM   sales      AS s
JOIN   customers  AS c  ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN   times      AS t  ON s.time_id   = t.time_id
WHERE  co.country_name  = 'France'
  AND  t.calendar_year  IN (2019, 2020)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same as #5 but additionally making sure the promo and channel rows satisfy the “total_id = 1” filters.
SELECT DISTINCT s.cust_id,
       s.time_id,
       s.amount_sold
FROM   sales       AS s
JOIN   customers   AS c   ON s.cust_id  = c.cust_id
JOIN   countries   AS co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN   promotions  AS p   ON s.promo_id = p.promo_id
JOIN   channels    AS ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
JOIN   times       AS t   ON s.time_id = t.time_id
WHERE  co.country_name    = 'France'
  AND  p.promo_total_id   = 1
  AND  ch.channel_total_id = 1
  AND  t.calendar_year     IN (2019, 2020)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate: monthly total amount_sold (local currency) for France in 2019.
SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS month,
       SUM(s.amount_sold)      AS total_local
FROM   sales      AS s
JOIN   customers  AS c   ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN   promotions AS p   ON s.promo_id = p.promo_id
JOIN   channels   AS ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
JOIN   times      AS t   ON s.time_id = t.time_id
WHERE  co.country_name      = 'France'
  AND  p.promo_total_id     = 1
  AND  ch.channel_total_id  = 1
  AND  t.calendar_year      = 2019
GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. The same aggregation for 2020, but also bring in the USD conversion factor.
SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS month,
       SUM(s.amount_sold * cu.to_us) AS total_usd
FROM   sales      AS s
JOIN   customers  AS c   ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN   promotions AS p   ON s.promo_id = p.promo_id
JOIN   channels   AS ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
JOIN   times      AS t   ON s.time_id = t.time_id
JOIN   currency   AS cu  ON cu.country = co.country_name
                         AND cu.year   = t.calendar_year
                         AND cu.month  = t.calendar_month_number
WHERE  co.country_name      = 'France'
  AND  p.promo_total_id     = 1
  AND  ch.channel_total_id  = 1
  AND  t.calendar_year      = 2020
GROUP BY t.calendar_month_number
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Calculate the average monthly sales (USD) for each year 2019 and 2020 side‑by‑side.
SELECT t.calendar_year                 AS year,
       AVG(s.amount_sold * cu.to_us)   AS avg_monthly_usd
FROM   sales      AS s
JOIN   customers  AS c   ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
JOIN   countries  AS co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
JOIN   promotions AS p   ON s.promo_id = p.promo_id
JOIN   channels   AS ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
JOIN   times      AS t   ON s.time_id = t.time_id
JOIN   currency   AS cu  ON cu.country = co.country_name
                         AND cu.year   = t.calendar_year
                         AND cu.month  = t.calendar_month_number
WHERE  co.country_name      = 'France'
  AND  p.promo_total_id     = 1
  AND  ch.channel_total_id  = 1
  AND  t.calendar_year      IN (2019, 2020)
GROUP BY t.calendar_year
ORDER BY year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Sketch of the full projection logic up to the median of projected 2021 monthly averages (result limited for inspection).
WITH hist AS (
    -- Monthly totals 2019 & 2020 in USD
    SELECT t.calendar_year  AS yr,
           t.calendar_month_number AS mo,
           SUM(s.amount_sold * cu.to_us) AS total_usd
    FROM   sales      AS s
    JOIN   customers  AS c   ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
    JOIN   countries  AS co  ON c.country_id = co.country_id
    JOIN   promotions AS p   ON s.promo_id = p.promo_id
    JOIN   channels   AS ch  ON s.channel_id = ch.channel_id
    JOIN   times      AS t   ON s.time_id = t.time_id
    JOIN   currency   AS cu  ON cu.country = co.country_name
                             AND cu.year   = t.calendar_year
                             AND cu.month  = t.calendar_month_number
    WHERE  co.country_name      = 'France'
      AND  p.promo_total_id     = 1
      AND  ch.channel_total_id  = 1
      AND  t.calendar_year      IN (2019, 2020)
    GROUP BY yr, mo
),
growth AS (
    -- Compute growth rate from 2019 to 2020 for each month
    SELECT h19.mo,
           (h20.total_usd - h19.total_usd) * 1.0 / NULLIF(h19.total_usd, 0) AS growth_rate
    FROM   hist AS h19
    JOIN   hist AS h20
           ON h19.mo = h20.mo
          AND h19.yr = 2019
          AND h20.yr = 2020
),
proj_2021 AS (
    -- Apply growth to 2020 numbers to project 2021
    SELECT h20.mo,
           h20.total_usd * (1 + IFNULL(g.growth_rate, 0)) AS projected_usd
    FROM   hist  AS h20
    LEFT JOIN growth AS g ON h20.mo = g.mo
    WHERE h20.yr = 2020
),
monthly_avg AS (
    -- Average per sale in projected 2021 (uses same count as 2020)
    SELECT p.mo,
           (p.projected_usd / NULLIF(cnt.cnt, 0)) AS avg_sale_usd
    FROM  proj_2021 AS p
    JOIN (SELECT t.calendar_month_number AS mo,
                 COUNT(*) AS cnt
          FROM   sales AS s
          JOIN   customers AS c  ON s.cust_id = c.cust_id
          JOIN   countries AS co ON c.country_id = co.country_id
          JOIN   times     AS t  ON s.time_id = t.time_id
          WHERE  co.country_name = 'France'
            AND  t.calendar_year = 2020
          GROUP BY mo) AS cnt
      ON cnt.mo = p.mo
),
median_calc AS (
    SELECT avg_sale_usd
    FROM   monthly_avg
    ORDER BY avg_sale_usd
    LIMIT 1 OFFSET 5   -- quick “median of 12” trick for inspection (not final)
)
SELECT *
FROM median_calc
LIMIT 20;
```

The last query is only an illustrative blueprint showing how the complete answer could be derived; tweak the LIMIT/OFFSET logic to obtain an exact median once all months are present.
